  "goodToKnow": "Spießig means petty-bourgeois, square or stuffy: obsessed with order, conformity and respectability, like a perfectly trimmed hedge and garden gnomes. Der Spießer or Spießbürger comes from medieval townsmen armed with a Spieß (pike). Synonyms: kleinbürgerlich, bieder, engstirnig. Being called spießig is an insult, though some ironically embrace it."
